  "Logs bundle saved to Downloads — a summary was copied to the clipboard. Paste it in the Slack thread and drag the zip in.": "日志包已保存到“下载”——摘要已复制到剪贴板。请将其粘贴到 Slack 会话中，并把 zip 文件拖入。",
  "Logs from": "日志来自",
  "Long cells are shortened": "较长的单元格会被截短",
  "Long prompts or documents may take multiple minutes to respond": "过长的提示词或文档可能需要几分钟才能响应",
  "Long sessions, big projects, and heavy Opus use. The free plan covers a fraction of this.": "长会话、大项目、大量使用 Opus。免费套餐只能覆盖其中一小部分。",
  "Longer chats draw down your usage faster": "更长的聊天会更快消耗你的用量",
  "Longer sessions are more expensive even when cached. /compact mid-task, /clear when switching to new tasks.": "更长的会话即使被缓存也更昂贵。任务中途用 /compact，切换到新任务时用 /clear。",
  "Longest streak": "最长连续记录",
  "Look at how my calendar has shifted this month compared to last": "看看我的日历这周相比上个月发生了哪些变化",
  "Look at my Airtable bases and give me a tour: what each one tracks, roughly how big it is, and which look actively used versus abandoned. Tell me which base we should work in first.": "查看我的 Airtable 库并给我做一个介绍：每个库跟踪的是什么、大致规模如何、哪些看起来在活跃使用而哪些已被搁置。告诉我应该先在哪个库里工作。",
  "Look at my Linear issues and give me the honest read: what’s urgent, what’s gone quiet, what’s probably obsolete, and what I should hand back or close. Ranked, with one-line reasons.": "查看我的 Linear 问题并给我一个真实的评估：什么是紧急的、什么已经悄无声息、什么可能已经过时，以及我应该退回或关闭什么。按优先级排序，并附上一句话理由。",
  "Look at my Outlook calendar and walk me through my day: each meeting, the gaps, and what I should prepare before each one. Tell me which hour is my best shot at focused work.": "看看我的 Outlook 日历，带我过一遍今天的一天：每个会议、会议间的空档、每个会议前我应该准备什么。告诉我哪个时段最适合专注工作。",
  "Look at my calendar for this week and tell me, honestly, which meetings could have been emails — and what each one is costing me in focus time. I want the version a candid friend would give me.": "看看我这周日历，老实告诉我，哪些会议本可以是一封邮件——以及每个会议消耗了我多少专注时间。我想要的是一个真心朋友会说的那种版本。",
  "Look at my closed deals from this quarter and tell me what the wins had in common, what the losses had in common, and the one thing the pattern says I should do differently.": "分析我本季度已关闭的交易，告诉我赢的单子有什么共同点、输的单子有什么共同点，以及这个模式表明我该在哪一件事上换种做法。",
  "Look at my connected calendar and inbox and propose three recurring tasks worth adding to the ones I already run: what each would do, when it would run, and what I’d stop doing by hand. Then run a sample of your best suggestion right now so I can see real output, and set up only the ones I approve.": "查看我已连接的日历和收件箱，提出三个值得加入我现有任务清单的周期性任务：每个任务做什么、什么时候运行，以及我会因此停掉哪些手动工作。然后立即运行你最佳建议的一个示例，让我看到真实输出，并只设置我批准的那些。",
  "Look at my docs and tell me what kind of genre writer I could be": "看看我的文档，告诉我我可以成为哪种类型的流派作家",
  "Look at my most active base and tell me something I probably haven’t noticed: a trend, an outlier, a column nobody fills in, or a pattern worth acting on. Surprise me with my own data.": "查看我最活跃的数据库，告诉我一些我可能没注意到的东西：一个趋势、一个异常值、一个没人填的列，或一个值得采取行动的模式。用我自己的数据给我惊喜。",
  "Look at my recently edited files, pick the three I was most actively working on, and tell me where I left off in each — plus the obvious next step to finish it. Help me restart without rereading everything.": "查看我最近编辑过的文件，挑出我最为活跃地处理过的三个，告诉我每个文件我停在了哪里——以及完成它的明显下一步。帮我重新开始，而不必重新阅读所有内容。",
  "Look at my scattered notes and propose a clean page structure for them — what groups together, what the hierarchy should be, what to archive. Show me the plan first; reorganize only after I approve.": "看看我散乱的笔记，为它们提出一个清晰的页面结构——哪些应该归在一起、层级应该怎样、哪些该归档。先给我看方案；只有在我同意后才重新整理。",
  "Look at my sent mail from the past two weeks and find up to three threads where I asked for something and never heard back. Draft a short, friendly nudge for each and save them as Gmail drafts, ready to send.": "查看我过去两周发送的邮件，找出最多三个我提出了请求但一直没有回复的会话。为每个会话草拟一封简短友好的催促邮件，并保存为 Gmail 草稿，随时可发送。",
  "Look at my two most active projects and find up to five tasks that haven’t moved in weeks but look like they’re holding other work up. For each, name the likely blocker and the person I’d need to nudge.": "查看我最活跃的两个项目，找出最多五个已经几周没有进展、但看起来正在阻塞其他工作的任务。对于每一个，说出可能的阻塞因素以及我需要去推动的那个人。",
  "Look at the commits from the last 24 hours. Summarize what changed, call out any risky patterns or missing tests, and note anything worth following up on.": "看看过去 24 小时的提交。总结一下改动了什么，指出任何风险模式或缺失的测试，并记下任何值得跟进的事项。",
  "Look at tomorrow’s meetings and draft a short agenda for each one I organize: purpose, three talking points, and the decision we need to leave with. Give them to me ready to paste into the invites.": "查看明天的会议，为我组织的每一个草拟一份简短的议程：目的、三个讨论要点，以及我们需要达成的决策。把它们准备好，可以直接粘贴到邀请函中。",
  "Look at what’s actually in my Drive and propose a folder structure that would make it findable — show me the plan as a simple tree, with where my existing files would go. Don’t move anything; just show me.": "查看我的 Drive 里实际有什么，提出一种能让内容易于查找的文件夹结构——以简单的树状图向我展示这个方案，并标出我现有文件会放在哪里。不要移动任何东西；只是给我看。",
  "Look over my code and give me tips": "查看我的代码并给我建议",
  "Look through my email from the past week and find the three replies I most owe people — questions that stopped at me. For each, tell me who’s waiting, how long they’ve waited, and the one-line gist of what they need.": "浏览我过去一周的邮件，找出我最欠别人的三条回复——那些在我这里停滞的问题。对于每一条，告诉我谁在等、等了多久，以及他们需要什么的一句话概要。",
  "Look through my emails and tell me where I’m avoiding something important": "翻翻我的邮件，告诉我我在哪些重要事情上有所回避",
  "Look through my recent Canva designs and give me a quick tour: what I tend to make, what’s working visually, and one concrete improvement you’d make to each of my three most recent designs.": "浏览我最近的 Canva 设计并给我一个快速概览：我倾向于制作什么、在视觉上哪些效果好，以及你对我最近三个设计中每一个会做的具体改进。",
